# Rental passive-loss limits

Rental depreciation is not an uncapped household deduction. `applyRentalPassiveLoss`
in `project.ts` applies federal passive-activity treatment, then
`deductions.depreciation` is only the amount that actually reduced income.

## Rules

Per rental (rent this year > 0): activity result = rent − opex − mortgage
interest − current-year straight-line depreciation − prior-year suspended loss.

- Gains on one property first offset losses on others.
- Leftover loss offsets other income only if `Household.realEstateProfessional`
  is true, or via the $25,000 active-participation allowance
  (`RealEstate.activeParticipation`, default true).
- The allowance phases out $0.50 per $1 of MAGI from $100k to $150k
  (`RENTAL_LOSS_*` in `federalTax.ts`). Constants are not inflation-adjusted.
- Disallowed loss carries forward on that same property
  (`rentalLossCarryforward` / `rentalLossCarryforwardById` on each row).
- No rent this year: no depreciation and no new loss. Prior carryforward stays
  parked on the property.

## MAGI proxy

The engine has no full Form 1040. MAGI is non-rental federal ordinary (after
pre-tax deposits) + capital gains + leftover rental *gain* after netting.
Rental *losses* are excluded. Roth conversions stay in ordinary, so they can
phase out the $25k allowance.

## What we do not model

Property sales (suspended losses are not released), married filing separately,
hour-based material participation, or grouping elections.

## UI

- Per-property "I actively participate" on the real-estate step (default on).
- Household "Real estate professional" on the real-estate step (default off).
- Year-by-year table: "Real-estate depreciation" is the allowed amount;
  "Real-estate loss carryforward" is the year-end suspended total (per-property
  children when there is more than one property).
